HST Office: in a narrow window the ribbon's tabs never run under the menu button; every tab stays reachable.

Below about 850 px the tab row was wider than the room before the ≡ button: the last tabs were drawn under it
and the search box was pushed out. A tab that would end past the room the search box's magnifier needs is now
left off the row (not drawn, no clicks). It stays one step away: the ≡ menu lists the tabs left off first, and
the KeyTips (Alt) show their letters left of the ≡ button.

